    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "### Contributing guidelines\n\n- [X] I have read [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CONTRIBUTING.md)\n- [X] I have read [CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md](https://github.com/echasnovski/mini.nvim/blob/main/CODE_OF_CONDUCT.md)\n\n### Module(s)\n\nmini.trailspace\n\n### Description\n\nRight now, all the mini.trailspace module does is allow for the highlighting of trailing whitespace and removal of that and blank lines at the end of a buffer/file, through the use of Lua functions.\r\n\r\nI think it would be better if instead the highlighting features be removed, because they can already be done with vanilla (Neo)Vim options: by using `listchars`'s `trail` setting. In addition to that, I'd also think it would be better if, similar to [tidy.nvim](https://github.com/mcauley-penney/tidy.nvim), there would be an option to automatically set up an autocommand to format the file using the Lua functions upon writing the buffer. A command (and maybe keybind) to toggle between this feature being enabled and doing it manually.\r\n\r\nBTW thanks for this actually super cool and awesome plugin; I've managed to replace like 15+ plugins with just this one!",
    "closed_at": "2023-11-02T16:25:43Z",
